| A. Kacheri Office | TypeScript, React/Vite, Fastify daemon, SQLite, Git CLI, SSE | Reliable agent lifecycle, worktree isolation, safe merges; ownership locks require enforcement | 7–10 | 4: CLI adapters; Git/worktrees; task persistence; board/logs/diffs UI | 3 | Agent CLIs lack usable unattended execution; advisory locks cannot prevent conflicting writes |
| B. Kacheri Jury | TypeScript, React/Vite, Fastify, Git CLI, local agent subprocesses | Grounding findings in diff lines, handling malformed output, deduplicating verdicts | 3–4 | 4: diff/context extraction; role orchestration; verdict normalization; review UI | 4 | Local CLI automation unavailable; correlated reviewers produce convincing false confidence |
| C. Kacheri Docs-Office | Python/FastAPI, React, SQLite, Tesseract, PDF rasterizer, macOS launchd, ICS | Accurate dates from variable documents; reminders while app is closed | 4–6 | 4: ingestion/OCR; extraction/confirmation; document UI; scheduling/ICS | 4 | Unconfirmed OCR dates cause missed deadlines; email requires configured delivery |
| D. Kacheri Relay | TypeScript, Fastify, React, SQLite; user-provided tunnel | Preserving raw payloads and distinguishing exact replay from edited requests | 2–4 | 4: capture/storage; replay engine; payload diff/editor; inspection UI | 5 | External delivery needs ingress; edited signed payloads fail verification without signing secrets |
| E. Kacheri MockHouse | TypeScript, Fastify, React, SQLite, OpenAPI parser | Inferring relationships and realistic state transitions from sparse schemas | 3–5 | 4: schema import; CRUD/state; fault injection; configuration UI | 4 | Arbitrary business behavior cannot be inferred reliably; scope must stay CRUD-focused |

Pick: **D**, for its bounded scope, independently buildable modules, and easily verified capture/replay behavior.
